Per room (20 bytes): spawn point of the Ninja. 0 = random of the two room spawn points;
else 3 times in 4 the point given by bit 7 (clear = first point $4BAE/$4BC2, set = second
point $4BD6/$4BEA) and 1 time in 4 random.

V key: when the first character of screen row 0 is the blank $20, copies the 40-character credit
line "BRUCE LEE (C) 1984 DATASOFT REV.2 BY RJF" from version_banner into row 0 of game_screen;
otherwise fills row 0 with $20. Changes A, X.

Exit permission of actor X. Returns carry clear when the actor may leave: always in room 11; at the
left edge (X < $10) moving left ($4f5d,x); at the right edge (X > $a1) moving right ($4f60,x);
below Y $c5 while falling (state $0e); at the top (Y < $31) moving up ($4f57,x). Else carry set.

Room 8 frame handler. Each opening happens one time:
 - room 7 has no lanterns left and lantern $4E00 (row 7, column 6) is taken ($4E99): passage at row 7,
   column 14;
 - lanterns $4DF8 and $4DFC (row 3) taken ($4E9A): if lantern $4E04 is still present, the animated chars restart
   with direction 1; passage at row 7, column 25;
 - room 8 has no lanterns left and room 9 lanterns $4E11 and $4E15 are taken ($4E9B): passage at row 2,
   column 38 ($3AAA);
 - lantern $4E00 taken ($4E97): passage at row 10, column 1;
 - rooms 7 and 8 have no lanterns left ($4E98): passage at row 10, column 38.
Then slider 0 (row 5, columns 6-11), slider 1 (row 5, columns 27-32) and the animated chars.

Room 8 frame handler. Each opening happens one time:
 - room 7 has no lanterns left and lantern lantern_list_room8+8 (row 7, column 6) is taken (room_state_c):
   passage at row 7, column 14;
 - lanterns lantern_list_room8 and lantern_list_room8+4 (row 3) taken (room_state_d): if lantern
   lantern_list_room8+12 is still present, the animated chars restart with direction 1; passage at row 7,
   column 25;
 - room 8 has no lanterns left and the room 9 lanterns lantern_list_room9+8 and +12 are taken (room_state_e):
   passage at row 2, column 38 (open_passage_ledge_b);
 - lantern lantern_list_room8+8 taken (room_state_a): passage at row 10, column 1;
 - rooms 7 and 8 have no lanterns left (room_state_b): passage at row 10, column 38.
Then slider 0 (row 5, columns 6-11), slider 1 (row 5, columns 27-32) and animate_scrolling_chars.

Room 9 frame handler. One-time events:
 - lantern $4E09 (row 2, column 32) taken ($4E99): animated chars direction 1, restart;
 - lantern $4E0D (row 7, column 15) taken ($4E97): passage at row 7, column 23; direction 0, restart;
 - room 9 has no lanterns left ($4E98): direction 0, restart, sound, tile $18 (61 84 84 63) at row 2, column 35.
Every pass: the runner at row 12 moves right (columns 4-24, then back to 4) while lantern $4E11 or $4E15 is
present, otherwise left (then back to 24); slider 0 (row 5) and slider 1 (row 6), columns 16-20, second look;
the animated chars.

Room 9 frame handler. One-time events:
 - lantern lantern_list_room9 (row 2, column 32) taken (room_state_c): animated chars direction 1, restart;
 - lantern lantern_list_room9+4 (row 7, column 15) taken (room_state_a): passage at row 7, column 23;
   direction 0, restart;
 - room 9 has no lanterns left (room_state_b): direction 0, restart, play_open_sound, tile $18 (61 84 84 63)
   at row 2, column 35.
Every pass: the runner at row 12 moves right (columns 4-24, then back to 4) while lantern lantern_list_room9+8
or +12 is present, otherwise left (then back to 24); slider 0 (row 5) and slider 1 (row 6), columns 16-20,
second look; animate_scrolling_chars.

Wizard defeat sequence, $4E98 passes ($50 at the start):
 - random colours (colour 0 on the last pass) on the wizard area of colour RAM (lines 5-8 columns 11-28,
   lines 3-4 and 9-12 columns 14-25);
 - $F2 (the $D018 value of the play area) = $3E, or $3C at random while more than 16 passes are left,
   so the charset flickers;
 - sound $8B;
 - $4E9A toggles and the four wizard parts are drawn in that frame: tiles $47/$48 at row 3 column 12,
   $49/$4A at row 3 column 25, $4B/$4C at row 6 column 14, $4D/$4E at row 6 column 23.

Wizard defeat sequence, room_state_b passes ($50 at the start):
 - random colours (colour 0 on the last pass) on the wizard area of colour RAM (screen rows 5-8 columns 11-28,
   screen rows 3-4 and 9-12 columns 14-25);
 - room_vmcsb (the VMCSB value of the play area) = $3E (charset_wizard_flash), or $3C (charset_wizard) at
   random while more than 16 passes are left, so the charset flickers;
 - sound $8B;
 - room_state_d toggles and the four wizard parts are drawn in that frame: tiles $47/$48 at row 3 column 12,
   $49/$4A at row 3 column 25, $4B/$4C at row 6 column 14, $4D/$4E at row 6 column 23.

Room 15 frame handler. Each opening is drawn on two passes ($4E97-$4E99 start at 1):
 - lantern $4E5B (row 3, column 19) taken: tile $57 at row 3 and tile $58 at row 4, column 17, sound;
 - lanterns $4E5F, $4E63 and $4E6B taken: tiles $57/$58 at rows 3/4, column 23, sound;
 - room 15 has no lanterns left: tiles $59, $5A, $5B at rows 9, 8, 7, column 37, sound.

Room 15 frame handler. Each opening is drawn on two passes (room_state_a..c start at 1):
 - lantern lantern_list_room15 (row 3, column 19) taken: tile $57 at row 3 and tile $58 at row 4, column 17,
   play_open_sound;
 - lanterns lantern_list_room15+4, +8 and +16 taken: tiles $57/$58 at rows 3/4, column 23, play_open_sound;
 - room 15 has no lanterns left: tiles $59, $5A, $5B at rows 9, 8, 7, column 37, play_open_sound.

