Sprite pointers 0-7 (block number = address/64 - $200). Sprites 0-4 show the actor buffers ($06-$0A or $0B-$0F,
written by show_actor_sprites); in room 18 sprites 6 and 7 get $0D/$0E from launch_fireball0/launch_fireball1;
the title uses block $0F for the TM sprite.

Reset template for the music voice state $E100-$E12D (46 bytes), copied by music_reset_state:
transpose 0; tie 0,0,0; ticks 0,0,0; end tick $FF x3; gate ticks 7 x3; end reload $FF x3;
AD $11 x3; SR $97 x3; control $21 (sawtooth, gate) x3; articulation 0 x3; envelopes of instrument 0 x3.

What happens when the song ends (the title code sets 3): 0 = stop; bit 7 set = play song (value AND $7F);
bit 1 set = take the next playlist entry (bit 0 set = restart the playlist at its end, clear = stop);
else play the next song number (after music_last_song: bit 0 set = song 0, clear = stop).

Per-frame music player (music_api_play, from the title screen IRQ). Stops on music_stop_request; does nothing
while music_playing is 0; at the song end runs music_song_end_action. Every music_tempo frames (a tick)
it updates the three voices: each tick counter counts down; at 0 the gate goes off (unless tied);
when it reaches the end tick, the counters reload and music_voice_start_note plays the next note.

Effect streams. Each command: command byte 0-7, then its operands. Command 0 = end;
1 = duration, note; 2 = duration, note, control; 3 = duration, note, ADSR index, control;
4 = duration, note, ADSR index, pulse index, control; 5 and 6 = duration, note, pulse index, control;
7 = control. Duration in frames (0 = 256), note = index in note_freq_lo/hi.
Effect 0 ($80), footstep: 1 frame of noise. Requested on each step of a walk or climb animation
(any character, $1FC4).

